OL,3,GNEWSAChippy to retire after 50 years of
OL,4,Afrying
OL,5,
OL,6,FFive decades of frying will come to an
OL,7,Fend this weekend for a fish and chip
OL,8,Fshop owner who has become a focal point
OL,9,Fof his community.
OL,11,FJamie Stott left school at 16 to work
OL,12,Fin his parents' fish and chip shop, JR
OL,13,FStott in Outwell, Norfolk, in 1976.
OL,15,FThe Stott family is synonymous with the
OL,16,Findustry locally, with Stott's brother
OL,17,Frunning a shop in March,
OL,18,FCambridgeshire.
OL,20,FThe 66-year-old says trade is up and
OL,21,Fdown and now is the time to hang up his
OL,22,Fchip scoop.
